<Base title="About the project"><section class="detail shell"><a class="back-link" href={base+'/'}>← DISCOVER</a><div class="detail-header"><div class="eyebrow orange">THE MISSION / 001</div><h1>Scientific curiosity deserves <em>better context.</em></h1><p class="lead">Research Observatory is an independent reading room for emerging research, beginning with active galactic nuclei and the physics of black holes.</p></div><div class="reading-layout"><div class="article-body"><h2>What this site does</h2><p>We discover recent arXiv submissions, organize them by topic and maintain an archive. The aim is to bring important studies to the surface, while keeping the boundary between scientific findings, authors' claims and editorial explanations visible.</p><h2>How papers are selected</h2><p>An automated collector searches relevant arXiv categories and ranks potential matches using transparent keyword rules. Ranking is a discovery aid, not a scientific quality score. New entries may be metadata-only until an editor has examined them.</p><h2>Our evidence standards</h2><p>Each record indicates whether it is based on abstract metadata or a curated review. We do not automatically turn an abstract into verified scientific conclusions. Numerical results, limits and uncertainty belong in source-linked technical notes.</p><h2>Publication and provenance</h2><p>Paper titles, authors, identifiers and dates come from arXiv. The original paper remains the authoritative source. Preprints should not be mistaken for peer-reviewed publications. The website is not affiliated with or endorsed by arXiv.</p><h2>What's next?</h2><p>Future versions may add more fields, evidence-linked result extraction, relationships between papers, and optional multilingual explanations. Private working notes remain separate from public material.</p></div><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sidebar-title">SOURCE & CODE</div><a href="https://github.com/yukawa1/research-observatory" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository ↗</a><br/><br/><a href="https://arxiv.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">arXiv ↗</a><hr/><div class="sidebar-title">CURRENT SCOPE</div><p>AGN · Spectroscopy · BLR · Variability · Baldwin effect</p></aside></div></section></Base>